"}\n"
"\n"

#. type: multicols
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:365
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\columnbreak\n"
"\\pagetarget{Artifact}{\\subheader{Artifact Cards}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\columnbreak\n"
"\\pagetarget{Artifact}{\\subheader{Cartes Artefact}}\n"
"\n"

#. type: multicols
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:372
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Artifact cards\\index{Artifact cards} have a top and bottom effect. When you play one, you must \\textbf{choose which effect} you are using.\n"
"They are divided into 3 Levels: Minor, Major, and Relic, with different border color.\n"
"These Levels relate to the overall Power of the card and may be referenced when resolving certain effects or during Scenario setup.\n"
"Otherwise, all Artifact cards are normally shuffled together to form the Artifact Deck regardless of their Level.\n"
"They are gained through map exploration.\\par\n"
"You can \\pagelink{Trading}{trade Artifacts with your allies} in Alliance and Cooperative \\mbox{Scenarios}.\\par\n"
"\\begin{tikzpicture}\n"
msgstr ""
"Les cartes Artefact\\index{Artifact cards} ont un effet en haut et un effet en bas. Lorsque vous en jouez une, vous devez \\textbf{choisir quel effet} vous utilisez.\n"
"Elles sont réparties en 3 niveaux : Mineur, Majeur et Relique, avec des bordures de couleurs différentes.\n"
"Ces niveaux correspondent à la Puissance globale de la carte et peuvent être cités lors de la résolution de certains effets ou pendant la mise en place du scénario.\n"
"Sinon, toutes les cartes Artefact sont normalement mélangées pour former la pioche d’Artefacts, quel que soit leur niveau.\n"
"Elles s’obtiennent en explorant le plateau.\\par\n"
"Vous pouvez \\pagelink{Trading}{échanger des Artefacts avec vos alliés} dans les scénarios Alliance et Coopératifs.\\par\n"
"\\begin{tikzpicture}\n"

#. type: multicols
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:392
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  \\node (major) {\\includegraphics[width=0.6\\linewidth]{\\cards/artifact.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{major}\n"
"    \\draw (0.2, 0.8) node {\\encircle{1}};\n"
"    \\draw (0.7, 0.4) node {\\encircle{2}};\n"
"    \\draw (0.9, 0.9) node {\\encircle{3}};\n"
"    \\draw (0.25, 0.2) node {\\encircle{4}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"  \\node [below=0pt of major.south] {\\imagecaption{Major Artifact}};\n"
"  \\node (relic) [right=0.05\\linewidth of major.south east, anchor=south west] {\\includegraphics[width=0.3\\linewidth]{\\cards/relic_artifact.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{relic}\n"
"    \\draw (0.5, 0.7) node {\\encircle{3}};\n"
"    \\node [below=0pt of relic.south] {\\imagecaption{Relic Artifact}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"  \\node (minor) [above=4em of relic.north] {\\includegraphics[width=0.3\\linewidth]{\\cards/minor_artifact.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{minor}\n"
"    \\draw (0.5, 0.7) node {\\encircle{3}};\n"
"    \\node [below=0pt of minor.south] {\\imagecaption{Minor Artifact}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"\\end{tikzpicture}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  \\node (major) {\\includegraphics[width=0.6\\linewidth]{translations/assets/fr/cards/artifact_fr.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{major}\n"
"    \\draw (0.9, 0.9) node {\\encircle{4}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"  \\node [below=0pt of major.south] {\\imagecaption{Artefact majeur}};\n"
"  \\node (relic) [right=0.05\\linewidth of major.south east, anchor=south west] {\\includegraphics[width=0.3\\linewidth]{translations/assets/fr/cards/relic_artifact_fr.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{relic}\n"
"    \\draw (0.5, 0.7) node {\\encircle{4}};\n"
"    \\node [below=0pt of relic.south] {\\imagecaption{Artefact Relique}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"  \\node (minor) [above=4em of relic.north] {\\includegraphics[width=0.3\\linewidth]{translations/assets/fr/cards/minor_artifact_fr.png}};\n"
"  \\begin{relcoords}{minor}\n"
"    \\draw (0.5, 0.7) node {\\encircle{4}};\n"
"    \\node [below=0pt of minor.south] {\\imagecaption{Artefact mineur}};\n"
"  \\end{relcoords}\n"
"\\end{tikzpicture}\n"
"\n"

#. type: multicols
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:402
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{multicols}{2}\n"
"  \\footnotesize\n"
"  \\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{1.}] Name\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{2.}] Effect\n"
"    \\columnbreak\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{3.}] Level\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{4.}] Flavor text\n"
"  \\end{itemize}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{multicols}{2}\n"
"  \\footnotesize\n"
"  \\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{1.}] Nom\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{2.}] Effet\n"
"    \\columnbreak\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{3.}] Texte narratif\n"
"    \\item[\\textbf{4.}] Niveau\n"
"  \\end{itemize}"

#. type: center
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:409
msgid ""
"{\\transparent{0.2}\\includegraphics[width=0.9\\linewidth]{\\art/"
"diplomats_ring.png}}"
msgstr ""
"{\\transparent{0.2}\\includegraphics[width=0.55\\linewidth]{\\art/"
"diplomats_ring.png}}"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:414
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{stronghold}\n"
"\\pagetarget{Spell Scroll Cards}{\\subheader{Spell Scroll Cards}}\\index{Spell Scroll cards}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"{stronghold}\n"
"\\pagetarget{Spell Scroll Cards}{\\subheader{Cartes Parchemin de sort}}\\index{Spell Scroll cards}\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:419
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"During setup shuffle 10 of the Spell Scroll cards into the Artifact Deck.\n"
"Set the remaining 10 cards aside to form a Spell Scroll Deck.\n"
"Some locations or Scenario effects may call for them later.\n"
"\\vspace*{1em}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Pendant la mise en place, mélangez 10 des cartes Parchemin de sort dans la pioche d’Artefacts.\n"
"Mettez les 10 autres cartes de côté pour former une pioche de Parchemins de sort.\n"
"Certains sites ou effets de scénario peuvent y faire appel plus tard.\n"
"\\vspace*{1em}\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:429
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"    \\medskip\n"
"    \\centering\n"
"    \\includegraphics[width=0.7\\linewidth]{\\cards/spell_scroll.png}\\\\\n"
"    \\medskip\n"
"    \\begin{center}\n"
"         \\imagecaption{Spell Scroll card}\n"
"    \\end{center}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"    \\medskip\n"
"    \\centering\n"
"    \\includegraphics[width=0.45\\linewidth]{\\cards/spell_scroll.png}\\\\\n"
"    \\medskip\n"
"    \\begin{center}\n"
"         \\imagecaption{Carte Parchemin de sort}\n"
"    \\end{center}\n"
"}\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:435
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\vspace*{1em}\n"
"When you gain a Spell Scroll, place it next to your Hero Board, take the two top cards from the Spell Deck and place them face-down on the Spell Scroll.\n"
"You can look at these Spells at any time and they don't count toward your Hand \\svg{hand} Limit.\n"
"You can only have two Spell Scrolls at a time.\n"
"If you gain a third one, draw the new Spells normally and then decide whether to discard the newly gained Spell Scroll or replace one you already have (including all Spells on it).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\vspace*{1em}\n"
"Quand vous gagnez un Parchemin de sort, placez-le à côté de votre fiche de Héros, prenez les deux premières cartes de la pioche de Sorts et posez-les face cachée sur le Parchemin de sort.\n"
"Vous pouvez regarder ces sorts à tout moment et ils ne comptent pas dans votre limite de cartes \\svg{hand}.\n"
"Vous ne pouvez avoir que deux Parchemins de sort à la fois.\n"
"Si vous en gagnez un troisième, piochez normalement les nouveaux sorts, puis décidez de défausser le Parchemin de sort que vous venez de gagner ou d’en remplacer un que vous possédez déjà (avec tous les sorts qu’il porte).\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:445
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can play Spells from a Spell Scroll like any other Spell with the following exceptions:\n"
"\\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item They don't count towards your Spell Limit.\n"
"    You can also play a Spell from your hand during this Combat Round.\n"
"    \\item You may use the Spell's \\textbf{lowest Power} \\svg{empower} \\textbf{effect}, without needing to pay its cost (e.g. in case of \\wikilink{spells/implosion}{Implosion} the cost is 1).\n"
"      You can't empower the Spell with \\svg{empower} from any source.\n"
"\\end{itemize}"
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez jouer les sorts d’un Parchemin de sort comme n’importe quel autre sort, avec les exceptions suivantes :\n"
"\\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item Ils ne comptent pas dans votre limite de sorts.\n"
"    Vous pouvez aussi jouer un sort de votre main pendant ce tour de Combat.\n"
"    \\item Vous pouvez utiliser l’\\textbf{effet de plus faible puissance} \\svg{empower} \\textbf{du sort}, sans avoir à payer son coût (par ex. pour \\wikilink{spells/implosion}{Implosion}, le coût est de 1).\n"
"      Vous ne pouvez pas augmenter le sort avec \\svg{empower}, quelle qu’en soit la source.\n"
"\\end{itemize}"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:453
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{stronghold}\n"
"    \\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item They can't be used to increase the \\svg{empower} of another Spell.\n"
"    \\item You can \\pagelink{selling Spell Scrolls}{sell Spell Scrolls} at a Trading Post for 2 \\svg{gold} per each Spell on it.\n"
"    \\item After using or selling those Spells, the Spell card is \\textbf{removed}, not discarded.\n"
"\\end{itemize}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"{stronghold}\n"
"    \\begin{itemize}\n"
"    \\item Ils ne peuvent pas être utilisés pour augmenter la \\svg{empower} d’un autre sort.\n"
"    \\item Vous pouvez \\pagelink{selling Spell Scrolls}{vendre des Parchemins de sort} à un Comptoir pour 2 \\svg{gold} par sort qu’ils portent.\n"
"    \\item Après avoir utilisé ou vendu ces sorts, la carte Sort est \\textbf{détruite}, et non défaussée.\n"
"\\end{itemize}\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:455
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the last Spell on a Spell Scroll is used or sold, place the Spell Scroll back in its Deck.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Si le dernier sort d’un Parchemin de sort est utilisé ou vendu, remettez le Parchemin de sort dans sa pioche.\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:458
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\medskip\n"
"Spell Scrolls are not part of your Deck, therefore they are not carried over between Scenarios in a Campaign."
msgstr ""
"\\medskip\n"
"Les Parchemins de sort ne font pas partie de votre deck ; ils ne sont donc pas conservés d’un scénario à l’autre dans une campagne."

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:463
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{rampart,cove}\n"
"  \\pagetarget{War Machines}{\\subheader{War Machine Cards}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"{rampart,cove}\n"
"  \\pagetarget{War Machines}{\\subheader{Cartes Machine de guerre}}\n"
"\n"

#. type: expansion
#: sections/deckbuilding.tex:467
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  War Machines\\index{War Machine cards} are permanent cards that can be bought at either a \\pagelink{Trading Post}{Trading Post} or a \\pagelink{War Machine Factory}{War Machine Factory}.\n"
"  If you buy one at the Trading Post, \\textbf{you cannot use} any of the other normal functions of that Field during that visit.\n"
"  War machines are also more expensive at the Trading Post.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"  Les machines de guerre\\index{War Machine cards} sont des cartes permanentes qui s’achètent à un \\pagelink{Trading Post}{Comptoir} ou à une \\pagelink{War Machine Factory}{Manufacture d’armes}.\n"
"  Si vous en achetez une au Comptoir, \\textbf{vous ne pouvez utiliser aucune} des autres fonctions normales de cette case pendant cette visite.\n"
"  Les machines de guerre sont aussi plus chères au Comptoir.\n"
"\n"

